1.REVERSE A STRING 
You are given a string s, and your task is to reverse the string.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static String reverseString(String s) {
                // code here
                char rev[]=s.toCharArray();
                for(int i=s.length()-1,j=0;i>=0;i--,j++){
                    rev[j]=s.charAt(i);
                }
                return new String(rev);
            }
            
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/reverse-a-string/1


2.CHECK FOR BINARY STRING 
Given a non-empty sequence of characters s, return true if sequence is Binary, else return false.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static boolean isBinary(String s) {
                for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++) {
                    if (s.charAt(i)!='0' && s.charAt(i)!='1') {
                        return false;
                    }
                }
                return true;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/check-for-binary/1


3.LONGEST WORD 
Given an array arr[] containing strings of names. Your task is to return the longest string. If there are multiple names of the longest size, return the first occurring name.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public String longest(List<String> arr) {
                String max=arr.get(0);
                for(int i=1;i<arr.size();i++){
                    if(arr.get(i).length()>max.length()){
                        max=arr.get(i);
                    }
                }
                return max;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/display-longest-name0853/1


4.REMOVE VOWELS FROM STRING 
Given a string s. Your task is to remove the vowels from the string.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            String removeVowels(String s) {
                StringBuilder ans=new StringBuilder();
                for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++){
                    char ch=s.charAt(i);
                    if(ch!='a' && ch!='e' && ch!='i' &&
                        ch!='o' && ch!='u'){
                        ans.append(ch);
                    }
                }
                return ans.toString();
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/remove-vowels-from-string1446/1
